inize him yesterday why are you so  confident in him in his job given that  you know he he said that the algorithm  was fine even though we saw what  happened  in scotland and in wales he also said  that kids didn't need to wear face masks  and now they do  is it because he's not good enough at  his job or is it because it is  a movable feast and we literally don't  know where this which direction this  virus is going to take us  i think on things like face coverings uh  where the government's introduced  guidance is in places where there are  localized lockdowns so it's not  surprising that we have tailored  advice uh in different parts of the  country depending  on the local health situation so this  really is an agile situation  i am confident of coursing in gavin as  say parliament's had their chance to  fully scrutinize him yesterday and i'm  sure there'll be future opportunities  there's a big mistake though wasn't it  the algorithm thing it was a big mistake  i think that uh all the uh nations in  the uk  took this approach on algorithm  initially uh with different regulators  and we've seen uh what's happening  consequence but generally is for gavin  and i have absolutely full confidence in  gavin taking this forward  i'm guessing we wouldn't use it again  though i think that uh there are all  sorts of ways that algorithms get used  in daily life  but you know offcourse already consulted  on proposals for next year they need to  consider them  but the most important thing is making  sure schools are fully reopened  and i'm really pleased how many schools  have taken on  uh the opportunity but with a phased  approach which is the right approach  um you know we all make mistakes um i  know you to be a compassionate woman i  just wanted you to  talk to me briefly about mercy  bergumer and for our viewers mercy was  a woman who died of starvation in  scotland  her little baby was found crying next to  her you were asked  about it at the time you didn't want to  