p okay you said of course it was  in glasgow staying in scotland uh nicola  sturgeon  announcing yesterday a draft bill for a  new scottish independence referendum  do you think that boris johnson will  allow that to happen well i think  this is the first i've heard of it and  i'm just somewhat surprised  last week we saw that scotland has a  record deficit  uh the union bonus is about two thousand  pounds per person in scotland  i really struggle to understand why this  is the right time to be thinking about  independence referendum  we just huge economic recovery ahead of  us and as a consequence i'm just  surprised that this is seen as the top  priority right now  what you will have heard of uh is uh the  new lineup for strictly i bet you're a  fan of strictly aren't you  i like a bit strictly i bet you do what  do you make of  nicola adams dancing as the first  same-sex couple  well i think it's a new adventure for  the bbc um  they're used to breaking new ground uh  on on the dance floor  uh it'll be interesting to see who leads  and who doesn't yeah because you're not  in favor of same-sex marriage are you  well i  took the view at the time and i i'd  still hold to that i have a strong faith  background about what is a legal  partnership and what is marriage  um but that's not a question for today  i'm a great believer in living let live  but i'll as i say i'll be interested to  see who will you vote for nicholas i've  got the feeling that nicola adams may  well take the lead  will you vote for her um i'll see who  the contestants are there are a great  number of there  i'm quite a fan of caroline quentin as  well who is it  would you like to take part no okay on  that note it's good to see  you stay there for just a second i  appreciate you taking the time to join  us

